  "name": "05. Switch Node",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "05. Switch Node is a workflow controls workflow designed to demonstrate reusable control and annotation nodes using the models configured in the graph. Its 10-node graph exposes 3 prompt/text field(s), 2 media input target(s), and 1 save/preview stage(s), while preserving the original editor-format graph for reference. The ComfyUI editor graph was converted to API format and is ready for live validation against the connected node and model registry.",
  "category": "Prompting & Language",
  "subcategory": "Workflow controls",
  "episode": "EP18",
  "instructions": "1. Open the workflow and select Validate. SineForge will compare every node class and input against the currently connected ComfyUI instance without queueing it.\n2. Confirm that any model selectors in the editable inputs resolve to files available in the main ComfyUI installation.\n3. Upload and assign the required image, mask, video, or audio files to the listed media inputs. Keep the source dimensions and duration appropriate for the selected model.\n4. Edit the source text or media, review the system/instruction fields, and inspect the generated text before passing it into another generation workflow.\n5. Save a copy before making structural changes. Use Editable inputs for normal parameters and Raw API JSON only when you need to inspect or change graph wiring.\n6. Validate again after every change. Queue one workflow only after validation passes; then inspect the returned output, logs, duration, dimensions, and media integrity.",
  "tags": [
    "EP18",
    "Prompting & Language",
    "Workflow controls"
  ],
